[0.001, "o", "23XX_ADC_CHANNEL0=y\u001b[m, but omits \u001b[94mCONFIG_ANALOG=y\u001b[m. In \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jked6c08d2f9152c1b;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/nuttx/drivers/analog/Kconfig#L6-L20\u0007nuttx/drivers/analog/Kconfig:6-20\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007, \u001b[94mconfig ADC\u001b[m is\r\n\u001b[6Cnested inside \u001b[94mif ANALOG\u001b[m (\u001b[94mmenuconfig ANALOG\u001b[m, \u001b[94mdefault n\u001b[m). Without \u001b[94mCONFIG_ANALOG=y\u001b[m, \u001b[94molddefconfig\u001b[m drops\n\u001b[92D\u001b[94mADC=y\u001b[m and \u001b[94m/dev/adc0\u001b[m is never compiled or registered.\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[1mAI Suggestion:\u001b[m \u001b[94mPROPOSE FIX\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[1mExplanation & Justification:\u001b[m Removing the non-existent \u001b[94mCONFIG_PWM_MULTICHAN=y\u001b[m symbol and adding \u001b[94mCONFIG_ANALOG=y\u001b[m\r\n  ensures \u001b[94m./tools/configure.sh -l ../xiao-rp2350-bargraph/board/configs/bargraph\u001b[m succeeds with zero Kconfig warnings\r\n  and compiles both the upper-half and lower-half ADC and multi-channel PWM drivers.\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[1mProposed Edit:\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n      • Location: \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkfbeb8fa296b1c746;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/docs/d"]
