[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[32A      \u001b[94mboards/arm/rp23xx/common\u001b[m calls \u001b[94mboard_autoled_*\u001b[m, \u001b[94mboard_userled_*\u001b[m, or \u001b[94mrp23xx_dev_gpio_init()\u001b[m when those options\u001b[K\r\n      are off (and \u001b[94mrp23xx_boardearlyinitialize()\u001b[m in \u001b[94mrp23xx_boardinitialize.c\u001b[m already initializes the onboard \u001b[94mGPIO25\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J\u001b[6CLED directly). Furthermore, \u001b[94mrp23xx_gpio.c\u001b[m from \u001b[94mxiao-rp2350\u001b[m hardcodes \u001b[94mGPIO26..28\u001b[m (\u001b[94mD0..D2\u001b[m), colliding with \u001b[94mADC0\u001b[m,\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mLED1\u001b[m, and \u001b[94mLED2\u001b[m.\n\u001b[15D2. \u001b[1mPWM Shutdown (\u001b[94;22mpwm_stop()\u001b[39;1m vs. \u001b[94;22mpwm_shutdown()\u001b[39;1m)\u001b[m: In \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk3056d941a3e11f67;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/nuttx/arch/arm/src/rp23xx/rp23xx_pwm.c#L643-L650\u0007nuttx/arch/arm/src/rp23xx/rp23xx_pwm.c:643-650\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007, \u001b[94mpwm_stop()\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6C(\u001b[94mPWMIOC_STOP\u001b[m) only clears \u001b[94m1 << priv->num\u001b[m in \u001b[94mRP23XX_PWM_EN\u001b[m (leaving the pad frozen while the descriptor remains\r\n\u001b[6Copen), whereas \u001b[94mclose(fd)\u001b[m invokes \u001b[94mpwm_shutdown()\u001b[m ("]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkacb42100e04bc909;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/nuttx/arch/arm/src/rp23xx/rp23xx_pwm.c#L249-L318\u0007nuttx/arch/arm/src/rp23xx/rp23xx_pwm.c:249-318\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007), which calls\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mpwm_stop()\u001b[m, configures \u001b[94mpin[0]\u001b[m and \u001b[94mpin[1]\u001b[m as outputs driven low (\u001b[94m0\u001b[m), switches their mux to \u001b[94mRP23XX_GPIO_FUNC_SIO\u001b[m,\r\n\u001b[6Cand zeros \u001b[94mpriv->duty[]\u001b[m.\r\n  • \u001b[1mAI Suggestion:\u001b[m \u001b[94mPROPOSE FIX\u001b[m\r\n  • \u001b[1mExplanation & Justification:\u001b[m Omitting \u001b[94mrp23xx_autoleds.c\u001b[m, \u001b[94mrp23xx_userleds.c\u001b[m, and \u001b[94mrp23xx_gpio.c\u001b[m from \u001b[94mxiao-rp2350-\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94mbargraph/board/src/\u001b[m (\u001b[94mCSRCS = rp23xx_boardinitialize.c rp23xx_bringup.c\u001b[m) eliminates ~750 lines of dead code and\r\n  removes the latent \u001b[94mGPIO26..28\u001b[m pin-mux collision. In \u001b[94mbargraph_shutdown_pwm()\u001b[m, zeroing the duties, issuing\r\n  \u001b[94mPWMIOC_STOP\u001b[m (which resets \u001b[94mupper->started = false\u001b[m in \u001b[94mdrivers/timers/pwm.c:428\u001b[m), and calling \u001b[94mclose(fd)\u001b[m (which invokes\r\n  \u001b[94mpwm_sh"]
[0.000, "o", "utdown()\u001b[m to drive the pins low via \u001b[94mRP23XX_GPIO_FUNC_SIO\u001b[m) guarantees every LED turns off cleanly without\r\n  needing an artificial \u001b[94musleep(2000)\u001b[m delay.\r\n  • \u001b[1mProposed Edit:\u001b[m\n\u001b[12D• Location: \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk3f96f7fdedd75cd;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/docs/designs/xiao-rp2350-bargraph.md#L23\u0007Line 23\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007, \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk1ae3085bc52490af;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/docs/designs/xiao-rp2350-bargraph.md#L108-L110\u0007Lines 108–110\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007, \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkf421d35213634ae3;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/docs/designs/xiao-rp2350-bargraph.md#L279-L280\u0007Lines 279–280\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007, \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk8146ab3f2673c1b2;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/docs/designs/xiao-rp2350-bargraph.md#L511-L520\u0007Lines 511–520\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007, \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk977b23c8c6ddf0b3;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/docs/designs/xiao-rp2350-bargraph.md#L545-L565\u0007Lines 545–565\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007, \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkb1817e36ed6cc909;"]
[0.000, "o", "file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/docs/designs/xiao-rp2350-bargraph.md#L658-L659\u0007Lines 658–659\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007\n\u001b[94D• Change:\n\u001b[5D• Remove \u001b[94mrp23xx_autoleds.c\u001b[m, \u001b[94mrp23xx_userleds.c\u001b[m, and \u001b[94mrp23xx_gpio.c\u001b[m from the directory tree (lines 108–110),\r\n\t  \u001b[94mboard/src/Make.defs\u001b[m (\u001b[94mCSRCS = rp23xx_boardinitialize.c rp23xx_bringup.c\u001b[m), and the Target Files list (former\r\n\t  items #18, #19, #20).\r\n\t  • Update Problem #5 (line 23), Section 4.2.4 (lines 279–280), and \u001b[94mbargraph_shutdown_pwm()\u001b[m (line 659) to\r\n\t  state that \u001b[94mpwm_stop()\u001b[m (\u001b[94mPWMIOC_STOP\u001b[m) only clears \u001b[94mRP23XX_PWM_EN\u001b[m while \u001b[94mclose(fd)\u001b[m invokes \u001b[94mpwm_shutdown()\u001b[m to\r\n\t  switch the pins to \u001b[94mRP23XX_GPIO_FUNC_SIO\u001b[m driven low (\u001b[94m0\u001b[m), so \u001b[94mbargraph_shutdown_pwm()\u001b[m writes zero duties,\r\n\t  calls \u001b[94mPWMIOC_STOP\u001b[m, and calls \u001b[94mclose(fd)\u001b[m without needing \u001b[94musleep(2000)\u001b[m.\r\n\n\n\n  How would you like to proceed with \u001b[1mItem 7\u001b[m? Please reply with \u001b[1mAccept proposed fi"]
