[0.000, "o", "mpered from \u001b[94m7J\u001b[m to the Red \u001b[94m+\u001b[m 3.3V rail).\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[1mAI Suggestion:\u001b[m \u001b[94mPROPOSE FIX\u001b[m\u001b[K\n\u001b[26D\u001b[1mExplanation & Justification:\u001b[m Ending the left-hand \u001b[94m+3.3V Rail\u001b[m line at \u001b[94mRow 1: +---[ Potentiometer Lug 1 (CW / 3.3V)\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94m]\u001b[m and showing \u001b[94mRow 7\u001b[m's \u001b[94m3V3\u001b[m jumper strictly on the right side (\u001b[94m7F\u001b[m / \u001b[94m7J\u001b[m -> Red \u001b[94m+\u001b[m 3.3V rail) eliminates any visual\u001b[K\r\n  ambiguity that could lead someone to wire the \u001b[94m3.3V\u001b[m rail to \u001b[94mD2\u001b[m (\u001b[94mGPIO28\u001b[m).\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[1mProposed Edit:\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n      • Location: \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkf27a180acb287c83;file:///Users/brett/Documents/GitHub/nuttxspace-egm/docs/designs/xiao-rp2350-bargraph.md#L174-L181\u0007Lines 174–181\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\n\tChange: Replace lines 174–181 with:\n\u001b[37D  \u001b[38;5;252m  Row 1: +---[ Potentiometer Lug 1 (CW / 3.3V) ]    |\u001b[m\n\u001b[47D\u001b[38;5;252m2: \u001b[4b[ Potentiometer Lug 2 (Wiper) ]-\u001b[7b+---> Jumper to Row 5A (D0/A0, GPIO26)\u001b[m\n\u001b[84D\u001b[38;5;252m3: \u001b[4b[ Potentiometer Lug 3 (CCW / GND) ]----+ \u001b[4b(Optional "]
[0.000, "o", "100 nF cap: Row 5B to GND)\u001b[m\n\u001b[92D\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[50X\u001b[50C|\u001b[m\u001b[K\n\u001b[34D\u001b[38;5;252mCols A..E \u001b[4bCenter    Cols F..J\u001b[m\n\u001b[50D\u001b[38;5;252mRow 5: \u001b[4b[D0/A0  GPIO26 (5E)]  ||  [(5F) 5V    ] (Unconnected)\u001b[m\n\u001b[60D\u001b[38;5;252m6: \u001b[4b[D1/A1  GPIO27 (6E)]  ||  [(6F) GND   ]+---> Jumper Row 6J to Blue (-) GND Rail\u001b[m\n\u001b[86D\u001b[38;5;252m7: \u001b[4b[D2/A2  GPIO28 (7E)]  ||  [(7F) 3V3   ]+---> Jumper Row 7J to Red (+) 3.3V\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\n\n  How would you\n\n\n\u001b[13D\u001b[?2026l"]
